%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel from the specification, pinned and not
endorsed, on the phantom links' path: the LOS state of the link from an
external or background cell to an indoor UE is drawn against the LOS
probability at the link's whole 2D distance, where the table takes the outdoor
part of it. ChannelModelIndoorLineOfSight pins the same on a real cell's link.

TR 38.901 v16.1.0 Table 7.4.2-1 ("LOS probability"), row UMa: "Pr_LOS = 1,
d2D-out <= 18m". Figure 7.4.1-2 has d2D = d2D-out + d2D-in.

Checked on a UMa background cell, on fifty indoor UEs 40 m from it on the
ground and 25 m inside their building, so d2D-out = 15 m. Each phantom link's
first evaluation draws its LOS state; the draw is replayed from a copy of the
model's generator. Every state is the draw against the probability at d2D =
40 m, 0.7415, and so some of the links are NLOS.
ChannelModelPhantomIndoorLineOfSightSpec asserts the specification as an
expected failure. When the model follows it, change this test together with
that one.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        channelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# the LOS state is drawn; the first number a link's first evaluation draws is its
**.dynamicLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *model = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "channelModel");
ChannelModelProbe probe(model);

// a UMa background cell's phantom radio, and fifty indoor UEs at one place: 40 m
// from it on the ground, 25 m inside their building, so 15 m of the 40 are outdoors
const int numUes = 50;
const double d2D = 40.0, d2DIn = 25.0;
StubEndpoint phantom;
phantom.nodeId = MacNodeId(900);
phantom.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
phantom.txPower = 46;
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubEndpoint>> ues;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    ues.push_back(std::make_unique<StubEndpoint>());
    ues[i]->nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ues[i]->coord = Coord(d2D, 0, 1.5);
    ues[i]->insideBuilding = true;
    ues[i]->insideDistance = d2DIn;
}

CellularTransmission transmission;
transmission.transmitter = &phantom;
transmission.phantomCell = this;
transmission.sourceId = phantom.nodeId;
transmission.cellId = phantom.nodeId;
transmission.direction = DL;
transmission.frameType = DATAPKT;
transmission.txPower = phantom.txPower;
transmission.startPosition = phantom.coord;
transmission.startTime = omnetpp::simTime();

const double d3D = phantom.coord.distance(ues[0]->coord);
// the strategy's LOS probability at the whole 2D distance, and at its outdoor part
const double pAtD2D = probe.pathLoss()->computeLosProbability(probe.deployment(25, 1.5), d3D, d2D);
const double pAtD2DOut = probe.pathLoss()->computeLosProbability(probe.deployment(25, 1.5), d3D, d2D - d2DIn);

wait(0.010);

// The first evaluation of each UE's phantom link draws its LOS state; the draw
// is replayed from a copy of the model's generator.
int numLos = 0, numAsAtD2D = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    probe.phantomPowerAt(transmission, ues[i].get());
    bool los = probe.losMap().at(LinkKey(phantom.nodeId, ues[i]->nodeId)).los;
    double u = omnetpp::uniform(snapshot.rng(), 0.0, 1.0);
    numLos += los;
    numAsAtD2D += (los == (u <= pAtD2D));
}

c.expectNear("the strategy's LOS probability at d2D = 40 m, for a 1.5 m UT", pAtD2D, 18.0 / 40 + std::exp(-40.0 / 63) * (1 - 18.0 / 40), 1e-12);
c.expectNear("...and at d2D-out = 15 m", pAtD2DOut, 1.0, 0);
c.expectValue("PINNED DEFECT: an indoor UE's phantom link is in the state of its draw against the probability at d2D, for every one of the links", numAsAtD2D, numUes);
c.check("PINNED DEFECT: ...so some of the links are NLOS, 15 m outdoors from the background cell", numLos < numUes, std::to_string(numLos) + " of " + std::to_string(numUes) + " in LOS");

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=4 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
